# English captions (seconds in the ORIGINAL recording NAF008.mp3). *word* = shown in gold.
# Cleaned by hand from TurboScribe (merged SRT source/NAF008.srt). Only the stretches used by the Shorts are captioned.
# 11:39-20:29 and 31:16-41:05 came back as Roman Urdu and were translated by hand: listen before publishing.
# Dropped by TurboScribe (retries pending, left out): 0:56-1:44, 12:07-12:33, 15:16-17:17, 27:11-27:41, 30:23-30:55.
# Left out on purpose: the misprint correction (11:31-11:39), the list of elders' names (19:40-19:49), the family
# aside about the children (25:18-25:32), and the remarks about other religions (39:28-40:08).
# "Sarkar" = the Prophet ﷺ (Hira, 11:49) or the shaykh (Khwaja Mian Sarkar) by context.
CAPTIONS = [
    # --- Short 1: Chilla-kashi
    (172.50, 185.60, "“*Chilla-kashi*.” A chilla means sitting for *forty days*: sitting for forty days, so that the worship done in them becomes a routine."),
    (186.40, 203.40, "To sit for forty days and worship Allah. In those forty days a special *blessing* descends; it becomes something very important, and for us it brings benefit both *inwardly* and outwardly."),
    (641.40, 657.60, "“At the beginning of the *wahi*”: in the days when revelation was coming to the Prophet ﷺ, he would go to *Ghar-e-Hira*, the cave of Hira."),
    (660.00, 669.40, "And he would take with him *provisions* that would not spoil for *eight days*."),
    (699.40, 708.60, "“Clearly, something that does not spoil for eight days cannot be *meat* or *ghee*.”"),
    (709.70, 718.80, "So the *Prophet* ﷺ took neither meat nor ghee. “From this comes *tark-e-haiwanat*”: giving up animal foods, both jalali and jamali."),
    (771.20, 775.60, "What is a *chilla*? It is *i'tikaf*."),
    (779.60, 791.40, "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat in *i'tikaf* in blessed *Ramadan*, and some of the Prophet's ﷺ blessed wives sat in i'tikaf too."),
    # --- Short 2: Saum-e-Maryam
    (792.30, 799.50, "Some of our *elders*, along with i'tikaf, also keep *Saum-e-Maryam*."),
    (809.30, 830.80, "Saum-e-Maryam: when, by Allah's command, Jibreel (A.S.) brought Bibi *Maryam* the *glad tidings* of a son, she said: “How can I have a child,"),
    (831.20, 837.00, "when no man has *touched* me?” But Allah does whatever He *wills*."),
    (837.40, 862.10, "So in this way Bibi Maryam came to be with child. Hers was a *prophet's* family: her uncle himself was a prophet. In a prophet's family, a child without marriage: people everywhere began to be *troubled*."),
    (862.10, 868.60, "And for Bibi Maryam, simply *living* became hard."),
    (868.60, 886.60, "In obedience to Allah's command: that is Saum-e-Maryam, which they keep. All day, while *fasting*, they speak to no one. Bibi Maryam spoke to no one; whatever was said to her, she did not *speak*."),
    (886.60, 894.50, "That is what Saum-e-Maryam is. That is why, in chillas, Saum-e-Maryam has its importance: *silence*."),
    # --- Short 3: Hizbul Bahr with fasting and silence (practice)
    (429.80, 449.90, "So, in the way of *Abdul Qadir Sahib Qibla*: if we are reading *Hizbul Bahr*, we fast for three days, or six days, or twelve days. This is explained in detail in the book."),
    (450.60, 461.50, "And what do we do in it? In the morning we first take a *bath*, then eat sehri, then pray Fajr, and begin reading *Hizbul Bahr*."),
    (461.60, 475.20, "At the time of Zuhr we pray Zuhr; at the time of Asr we pray Asr; and we keep on reading, until the fixed *count* is complete."),
    (476.10, 480.50, "But we do not *talk* to anyone. We talk to no one."),
    (481.30, 489.40, "At Maghrib we break the fast, pray Maghrib, and only *then* do we talk."),
    (1246.80, 1256.50, "Later, Hazrat *Khwaja Muhammad Siddiq* said: do it like this: keep *three fasts*."),
    (1259.50, 1271.90, "After the Fajr prayer, read *Hizbul Bahr* three times."),
    (1273.20, 1287.60, "Now you are fasting, but you may *talk*: go to the market, go to the office, go to the prayer, do everything. Only keep the *fast*."),
    (1419.80, 1426.10, "And the last permission, the one I am giving you, is the way of *Khwaja Mian Sarkar*."),
    (1446.80, 1460.90, "Khwaja Mian Sarkar: what *glory* is his, what a station, Allahu Akbar, that he made the practice of Hizbul Bahr *easy* for us."),
    # --- Short 4: Hazrat Musa Pasha and Hizbul Bahr
    (1336.30, 1348.10, "And in it there are very strict *mu'akkils*, the unseen beings attached to it. Very strict. Those mu'akkils trouble a person a lot; they *follow* him."),
    (1349.80, 1355.10, "When Hazrat came, the mu'akkils had no *courage*; they kept quiet."),
    (1361.30, 1377.50, "But Hazrat *Musa Pasha*, in his room, during the day, was reading Hizbul Bahr: reading, reading, one by one, keeping *count*."),
    (1378.90, 1388.50, "Then it came and lifted his *leg*. Hazrat Musa Pasha was left on one leg, the other held up like this."),
    (1391.60, 1406.00, "Now what could he do? He could not call out, he could not speak, he could not ask anyone for help: he was keeping *Saum-e-Maryam*. So he kept on reading Hizbul Bahr, reading and reading."),
    (1407.40, 1414.00, "In the end it *let go*. So you see what a thing *Hizbul Bahr* is."),
    # --- Short 5: I'tikaf and the thought on one point
    (1046.10, 1052.50, "Some elders sit in i'tikaf for a week, two weeks, three days. I'tikaf can be for even *one day*."),
    (1053.10, 1060.10, "For i'tikaf in the *Hanafi* madhab, fasting and being in a masjid are necessary."),
    (1062.00, 1071.00, "With the *Shafi'is*, i'tikaf can be for even a short while; the Shafi'is can do i'tikaf for a little time too."),
    (1072.40, 1096.90, "Everyone goes to the masjid. Make the *intention* of i'tikaf for an hour or two: what harm is there? When we go to the masjid for an hour or two and make the intention of i'tikaf, what is wrong with that? We *should* do it."),
    (1098.20, 1113.20, "“In i'tikaf a person is turned *wholly* toward worship. His thought becomes fixed on *one point*.”"),
    (1114.20, 1122.60, "“*Complete attention* is the soul of worship.” It is all about thought: *khayal*, only khayal."),
    (1123.50, 1145.30, "Now, what thought are you all in at this moment? Allah, Allah's Messenger ﷺ, the deen of Islam, the *awliya*, the elders of the deen, the prophets, Hazrat Zakariya and Bibi Maryam: all of them are being remembered. Our thought is engaged in *worship*."),
    (1146.90, 1161.00, "MashaAllah. “In i'tikaf a person is turned wholly toward worship; his thought becomes fixed on one point. *Complete attention* is the soul of worship.”"),
    (1162.20, 1179.60, "“In our time too, special servants of *Allah* spend two or three months in i'tikaf, and also keep *Saum-e-Maryam*.”"),
    # --- Short 6: Four shops in one namaz
    (1508.80, 1514.80, "There is no *benefit* in namaz with a scattered mind and without a *gathered* heart."),
    (1532.30, 1543.60, "There was a gentleman, a regular namazi, but he prayed with a *scattered* mind. He had four *shops*."),
    (1544.20, 1557.70, "In the first rakat he would go over the accounts of the first shop; in the second rakat, the second shop; in the third rakat, the third shop; in the fourth rakat, the *fourth shop*."),
    (1559.30, 1578.20, "Once, when the imam led the namaz, the man objected: “You prayed only *three* rakats! I haven't yet seen the account of my *fourth* shop.”"),
    (1579.70, 1598.90, "Do you understand? The imam said: “I prayed *four* rakats.” He replied: “I went over the first shop, the second, the third; but the account of the fourth shop I have not *seen*.”"),
    (1602.30, 1610.40, "Everyone *laughed*: he had been reading the *book of accounts*, not the book of the heart."),
    (1672.10, 1676.50, "There is no *benefit* in scattered thoughts, without the *heart*."),
    # --- Short 7: Fruit out of season
    (1876.10, 1895.90, "Hazrat *Zakariya* (A.S.) was the uncle of Hazrat Bibi Maryam. Bibi Maryam's father and mother had made a *vow*: if we are given a child, we will devote it to the service of Allah's house."),
    (1895.90, 1909.70, "Then they were given a child: a girl was born, Bibi *Maryam*. Now what were they to do?"),
    (1909.70, 1937.10, "When she reached that age, in that same place of worship, the place of worship of the Jews of that time, a room was set apart for Hazrat Bibi Maryam and made *sacred*, and she was left in it: “Now stay in here; stay in the *worship* of Allah.”"),
    (1937.10, 1954.90, "And Hazrat Zakariya and his blessed family would *look after* her: caring for her, watching over her. That is how it was."),
    (1955.60, 1971.20, "Hazrat Bibi Maryam was growing up; in time she reached a good age, mashaAllah. Then Hazrat Zakariya came to *ask after* her."),
    (1971.20, 1991.90, "Near her room the two were talking, when a strong *gust* of wind came. The curtain lifted, and as it lifted, Hazrat Zakariya's eyes fell *inside* the room."),
    (1991.90, 2002.60, "Hazrat Bibi Maryam had come out to meet her uncle. And what was there in the room? *Fruits*:"),
    (2002.60, 2021.40, "fruits that are not found in this season. The fruit of summer is one kind, of the rains another, of winter another; each season has its own. And there, fruits *out of season* were all there."),
    (2021.90, 2041.10, "Hazrat Zakariya said: “Maryam, where have these fruits come from? Where has fruit out of season come from?” She said: “*Allah* sends them to me. Allah *sends* them to me.”"),
    # --- Short 8: Where du'as are accepted
    (2069.00, 2092.40, "Then, standing *right there*, he said: “Ya Allah, You give Maryam fruit *out of season*. Now have mercy on me, be generous to me: give me a child out of season.”"),
    (2133.70, 2157.60, "Right there, as soon as he made du'a, Allah at once *accepted* it. Jibreel (A.S.) came and said: “Zakariya, Allah is going to give you a *son*; He has accepted your du'a. Now a son will be born to you.”"),
    (2157.60, 2177.20, "He said: at this age? Yes: the du'a he had just made was beside Bibi Maryam's room. She is a *waliya* of Allah; he made du'a near her, and Allah *accepted* it."),
    (2313.10, 2332.20, "So what is being taught here? The house of Allah is for *everyone*. But whomever Allah calls His wali, His *friend*, and is kind to: that is his honour,"),
    (2332.20, 2354.60, "his good fortune. As He gives Bibi Maryam fruit out of season, for Him there is no limit of *age*: He gives when He wills. He gave Yahya (A.S.) when Zakariya was a hundred and twenty, and in her ninetieth year his wife was with child."),
    (2354.60, 2369.40, "So the *court* of the awliya of Allah is a place of greatness, of Allah's *special kindness*."),
    (2409.10, 2438.90, "In the *Qur'an* we see: where Hazrat Bibi Maryam lived, Allah's grace was such that a prophet's du'a was accepted, in the court of a waliya of Allah. That is the station: the court of the awliya of Allah is the place where Allah *accepts* du'as. Keep this in mind."),
]
